Acknowledgements & Prior Art
----------------------------
M5Blade is an independent clean-room Swift implementation, informed by hardware research,
Apple Silicon SMC key discoveries, and architectural patterns from the following open-source
projects and authors:

- agoodkind/macos-smc-fan — Ari Goodkind
  https://github.com/agoodkind/macos-smc-fan
  Documented the Apple Silicon M5 (Tahoe) lowercase `F0md` vs uppercase `F0Md` SMC key casing
  discovery and modern `SMAppService.daemon` XPC architecture.

- exelban/stats — Serhiy Mytrovtsiy (MIT License)
  https://github.com/exelban/stats
  Reference for `AppleSMC` IOKit `SMCKeyData_t` 80-byte struct layout, `IOHIDSensor` fallback
  patterns, and Apple Silicon sensor key conventions.

- fermion-star/apple_sensors & vladkens/macmon — Vladislav K
  https://github.com/fermion-star/apple_sensors
  https://github.com/vladkens/macmon
  Reference for Apple Silicon `IOHIDEventSystemClient` thermal sensor enumeration and unprivileged
  `IOReport` power/residency telemetry.

- hholtmann/smcFanControl — Hendrik Holtmann (GPL-2.0, historical prior art only)
  https://github.com/hholtmann/smcFanControl
  Pioneered macOS `AppleSMC` user-client control selector (`kSMCHandleYPCEvent = 2`).

- macmade/Hot — Jean-David Gadina (MIT License)
  https://github.com/macmade/Hot
  Reference for combining `NSProcessInfo.thermalState` with `IOHIDEventSystem` temperature reads.

- alienator88/HelperToolApp & trilemma-dev/SwiftAuthorizationSample
  https://github.com/alienator88/HelperToolApp
  https://github.com/trilemma-dev/SwiftAuthorizationSample
  Reference patterns for `SMAppService.daemon(plistName:)` and XPC audit-token code-signing verification.

- Asahi Linux Project — Apple SMC Hardware Documentation
  https://asahilinux.org/docs/hw/soc/smc/
  Reference documentation for the Apple Silicon RTKit-based SMC mailbox architecture.
